<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kakheti</h1><p class="st-meta">1465 CE – 1762 CE · capital Gremi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The eastern Georgian kingdom of Kakheti, a land of vineyards and silk routes that suffered terribly under Shah Abbas before uniting with Kartli in 1762.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1465, amid the disintegration of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-georgia">Kingdom of Georgia</a>, George I, a prince of the royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagrationi-dynasty">Bagratid</a> house, made <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-kakheti">Kakheti</a> a separate kingdom. Its independence was confirmed when <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/georgia">Georgia</a> split into three kingdoms in 1490. His line, a branch of the Bagratids, held the throne of Kakheti for almost three centuries.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-kakheti">Kakheti</a> prospered on wine, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> and the caravan trade between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/shirvanshah-state">Shirvan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>; King Levan built a royal residence at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gremi">Gremi</a>. The kings balanced between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teimuraz-i-of-kakheti">Teimuraz I</a>'s resistance provoked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> to devastate the country in 1616, deporting many thousands of Kakhetians to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>; Teimuraz's mother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ketevan-the-martyr">Ketevan</a> was martyred in 1624.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-kakheti">Kakheti</a> endured Persian governors and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lezgins">Lezgin</a> raids. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erekle-ii">Erekle II</a> became king in 1744, and on his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teimuraz-ii-of-kakheti">Teimuraz II</a>'s death in 1762 he united Kakheti with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kartli">Kartli</a> as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kartli-kakheti">Kingdom of Kartli-Kakheti</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-kakheti.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Kakheti" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kingdom_of_Kakheti.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1465 CE – 1762 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gremi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Levan, Teimuraz I, Erekle II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Georgian Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Georgian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/georgia">Georgia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kakheti, Kakhetian Kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1614&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kakheti" aria-label="Kingdom of Kakheti on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5790 682 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Kakheti lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6110 938L6036 930M6110 938L6281 1235M6110 938L6298 1144M6110 938L6091 947"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6036 930h0M6281 1235h0M6298 1144h0M6091 947h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6110 938h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6110 938h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Gremi. <a href="/atlas?year=1614&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kakheti">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
